# Dock "Options → Assign To" desktop pins. macconfig-check.sh compares them; macconfig-check.sh --fix applies them
# (lib/desktop-bindings.py --apply) by writing com.apple.spaces app-bindings.
# Format (pipe-delimited): Display name | bundle id | desktop | optional manual step
#   desktop: 1..N = "This Desktop" on Desktop N of the main display; none = not assigned
#   Bundle ids are matched case-insensitively (macOS stores them lowercased).
#   Desktop N is resolved to that Space's current UUID when applying (Desktop 1 is "").
#   UUIDs for Desktops 2+ change if Spaces are recreated; they are not stored here.
#   YouTube Music is a Chrome web app with its own bundle id.
#   A bundle field that starts with @APP@ is an app path, not a bundle id.
#   @HOME@ in that path is $HOME. The bundle id is CFBundleIdentifier in the app's
#   Contents/Info.plist, read when checking or applying. A Safari web app's id
#   contains a UUID that is different on each Mac, so the UUID is not stored here.
#   If that app is not installed, the row is not set up yet (the optional fourth
#   field is the manual-step id). It is not drift, and --fix does not write a pin.
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
Slack|com.tinyspeck.slackmacgap|1
WhatsApp Web|@APP@@HOME@/Applications/WhatsApp Web.app|1|whatsapp-web
Granola|com.granola.app|1
Google Chrome|com.google.Chrome|2
Cursor|com.todesktop.230313mzl4w4u92|3
Cursor Nightly|co.anysphere.cursor.nightly|3
Grok Bot|com.anysphere.sand|3
Spotify|com.spotify.client|4
YouTube Music|com.google.Chrome.app.cinhimbnkkaeohfgghhklpknlkffjgod|4
Ghostty|com.mitchellh.ghostty|none
CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor|none
